{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>And now, come, my beloved, let us go out to the field, for we cannot be together in the city. And \"Who would give you to me as a brother\" — until I bring you publicly to my mother's house, and she will teach me how I would kiss you from spiced wine." "<b>The third time</b><br>(\"Who would give you to me as a brother.\" Knesset Israel says to the Messiah: Who would give you to me as a brother, and I would find you) and I would cling to you."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:00.089267272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}